MODEL WATCH #55 — Tuesday, September 15, 2026

1. FERRITE-70B (OPEN, APACHE 2.0): THE FULL TABLE
Best open model we have measured on structured work. Composite and per-family scores against the models it competes with on price:

  Model               Composite   Extraction   Tool use   Reasoning   $/M out (hosted)
  Ferrite-70B (open)     78.9        94.1        95.0       68.2       $1.80 (Kestrel)
  Quillon-L              78.4        89.1        91.2       77.6       $4.50
  Sable-3 Mini           74.6        86.4        90.5       71.9       $0.44
  Tanager-Coder 2        70.1        84.0        92.3       60.4       $0.68

On extraction it is within two points of the frontier models at a tenth of the price. Reasoning is where you still pay for proprietary. https://modelwatch.dev/models/ferrite-70b

2. LODESTONE-R2: -15%
Now $3.40 / $13.60 per million. Still the reasoning leader (94.8); still slow. R2 batch at half price with a 24-hour window is the way to run it for anything not interactive.

3. TANAGER-CODER 70B (PREVIEW)
Agentic coding 79.4 in preview, up from the 34B's 71.2 and now first among open models by a wide margin. 2x the price, 3x the latency of the 34B. Public release slated for October.

4. PRICE CHANGES THIS WEEK
  Lodestone-R2: -15%
  Kestrel, Ferrite-70B: new, $0.60 / $1.80
  Argent, Ferrite-70B: announced for this week

